{
  "id": 139705548,
  "iid": 6202,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: highlight when search result is in the current packet.",
  "description": "Calling setCurrentIndex with QItemSelectionModel::ClearAndSelect clears\nthe currentIndex, but not the selection, so it doesn't trigger\nselectionChanged. However, highlighting depends on the selectionChanged\nsignal, not currentChanged(), and it's not emitted if we're still on the\nsame packet/row as the current selection (which can occur if searching\nfor something that occurs in exactly one packet in a capture.)\n\nSince packet_list_select_row_from_data() cares about where the data\nis within the packet, it needs to clear the selection.  Fix #8269",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2022-02-11T01:23:29.369Z",
  "updated_at": "2024-08-02T21:56:00.230Z",
